---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title =
  "About Wakiee | Safe Voice, Video & Group Conversations";

const description =
  "Learn about Wakiee, our mission, values, privacy practices, safety systems, moderation approach, and commitment to providing secure voice, video, and group conversations in a respectful online community.";

const keywords =
  "about wakiee, wakiee owner,wakiee founder,talk to strangers, random video chat platform, voice chat strangers, online chat rooms, improve english speaking, build confidence online";

const canonical = "https://wakiee.live/about";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "About Wakiee",
      "url": "https://wakiee.live/about",
      "description":
        "Wakiee is a platform to talk to strangers through video and voice chat while building confidence and communication skills.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "@id": "https://wakiee.live/#website"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Wakiee",
        "url": "https://wakiee.live/",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://wakiee.live/android-chrome-192x192.png"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "https://wakiee.live/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "About",
          "item": "https://wakiee.live/about"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  robots="index, follow, max-image-preview:large"
  canonical={canonical}
  ogTitle="About Wakiee – Connect, Learn & Talk"
  ogDescription="Discover how Wakiee helps people connect globally, build confidence, and improve communication skills."
  ogImage="https://wakiee.live/android-chrome-192x192.png"
  ogUrl={canonical}
  ogType="website"
  twitterTitle="About Wakiee"
  twitterDescription="Learn about Wakiee and how it helps people connect worldwide."
  twitterImage="https://wakiee.live/android-chrome-192x192.png"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div
    style="padding: 40px 20px; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif;"
  >
    <!-- Outer Grey Border Container -->
    <div
      style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; border: 1px solid #2a2a2a; border-radius: 16px; padding: 20px; background: #0b0f1a;"
    >
      <!-- Inner Content Box -->
      <div
        style="border-radius: 12px; padding: 30px 20px; color: white; text-align: center;"
      >
        <!-- Banner with curved corners -->
        <img
          src="/banner.webp"
          alt="About Wakiee - Voice Chat, Video Chat and Group Conversation Platform"
          style="max-width: 100%; width: 340px; margin: 0 auto 30px; display: block; border-radius: 14px;"
        />

        <!-- Introduction -->
        <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 20px;">
          About Wakiee
        </h1>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Wakiee is a platform built to help people connect through real-time voice conversations, video calls, and group discussions in a respectful and secure environment. Our goal is to make online communication fast,simple, accessible, and meaningful by giving people an easy way to meet others, exchange ideas, practice languages, build confidence, and discover different cultures without unnecessary barriers.

          <br /><br />

          We believe online communication should be simple, respectful, and easily accessible while maintaining high standards of user safety, privacy, and transparency.That's why Wakiee is designed to provide instant access to conversations while maintaining a strong focus on privacy, user safety, and responsible community standards. Whether someone is looking to have a casual conversation, improve communication skills, meet people from around the world, or participate in community discussions, Wakiee provides multiple ways to communicate through <a href="/video" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Video Chat</a> , <a href="/voice" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Voice Chat</a> , and <a href="/rooms" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Group Voice Rooms</a> .

          <br /><br />

          Every feature is developed with the objective of creating a reliable platform where respectful conversations can take place. We continuously work to improve platform stability, safety systems, moderation tools, and the overall user experience so that people can communicate with greater confidence while following clear community standards and responsible online behaviour.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          Our Mission
        </h2>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Our mission is to create an online communication platform where people can safely connect across countries, cultures, and backgrounds through meaningful conversations. We aim to remove unnecessary barriers to communication while encouraging respectful interactions, personal growth, cultural exchange, and language learning.

          <br /><br />

          Wakiee is committed to building an environment where users feel comfortable starting conversations, sharing ideas, improving their communication skills, and forming genuine human connections. Alongside new features and continuous improvements, we remain focused on privacy, transparency, platform integrity, and responsible moderation to ensure that the community remains welcoming for everyone.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          Our Vision
        </h2>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Our vision is to build a trusted communication platform where people from around the world can connect through respectful conversations, meaningful discussions, and shared experiences. We believe online communication should encourage learning, cultural exchange, collaboration, and genuine human interaction while maintaining high standards of privacy and user safety.

          <br /><br />

          As Wakiee continues to grow, we are committed to improving the platform through better moderation technologies, stronger privacy protections, enhanced accessibility, and new communication features that create a safer experience for everyone. We regularly evaluate community feedback, platform performance, and emerging safety practices to guide future improvements.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          What Makes Wakiee Different
        </h2>

        <div
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto 40px; text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          <p>
            Wakiee is designed around a simple principle: meaningful conversations should be easy to start, safe to participate in, and accessible to everyone. Every feature is developed with user experience, privacy, and responsible community management in mind.
          </p>

          <ul style="padding-left: 22px; margin-top: 20px;">
            <li>
              <strong>Multiple ways to communicate</strong> through
              <a href="/video" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Video Chat</a>,
              <a href="/voice" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Voice Chat</a>, and
              <a href="/rooms" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Group Voice Rooms</a>.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Privacy-focused communication</strong> designed to minimize unnecessary personal information while encouraging responsible online interactions.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Safety-first approach</strong> supported by AI-assisted moderation, human review, community reporting, and platform enforcement tools.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Continuous platform improvements</strong> based on technical enhancements, user feedback, and evolving safety practices.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Global accessibility</strong> that allows people from different countries and backgrounds to communicate, learn, and exchange ideas.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Responsible community management</strong> supported by moderation systems, room management controls, and clearly defined community standards.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
            Our objective is not simply to connect people, but to create an environment where conversations remain respectful, productive, and enjoyable while maintaining high standards for privacy, safety, and community trust.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          Our Commitment to User Safety
        </h2>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Creating a safe and respectful environment is one of Wakiee's highest priorities. Every part of the platform is designed to encourage positive interactions while reducing abusive or disruptive behaviour. We continuously improve our moderation systems, platform tools, and community standards to help users communicate with greater confidence across the platform.
        </p>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Safety on Wakiee is supported through a combination of automated systems, AI-assisted moderation, human review, community reporting, and platform enforcement tools. While no moderation system can prevent every violation, we continuously monitor reports, improve detection methods, and update our policies to maintain a safer experience for everyone.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 35px;">
          Video Chat Safety
        </h3>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 15px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Video conversations are supported by moderation systems designed to identify behaviour that violates our Community Standards. Users can report inappropriate conduct directly from the platform, and reports may be reviewed through a combination of AI-assisted tools and human moderators. Depending on the severity of the violation, moderation actions may include warnings, temporary restrictions, or permanent bans.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 35px;">
          Voice Chat Safety
        </h3>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 15px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Voice conversations are expected to follow the same standards of respectful behaviour. Users are encouraged to report harassment, abusive language, threats, spam, or other violations. Reported behaviour may be investigated, and appropriate moderation action may be taken when our policies are violated.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 35px;">
          Group Voice Rooms Safety
        </h3>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 15px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Group Voice Rooms include additional moderation tools that help room owners maintain a respectful environment. Depending on room permissions, moderators or room creators may remove disruptive participants, temporarily mute users, lock rooms to control new participants, and manage ongoing discussions. These tools help communities maintain productive and respectful conversations while reducing spam and disruptive behaviour.
        </p>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          We encourage every member of the Wakiee community to help maintain a positive environment by reporting violations, respecting other users, and following our Community Guidelines. Community participation plays an important role in helping us improve the platform and maintain a welcoming experience for everyone.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          Community Standards & Responsible Behaviour
        </h2>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Wakiee is built to encourage respectful, friendly, and meaningful conversations. Every user shares responsibility for maintaining a welcoming environment where people can communicate safely and confidently. By using Wakiee, users agree to follow our <a href="/guidelines" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Community Guidelines</a>, <a href="/terms" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Terms of Service</a>, and all applicable laws.
        </p>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          The following behaviour is not permitted anywhere on the platform:
        </p>

        <div
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto 35px; text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          <ul style="padding-left: 22px;">
            <li>Harassment, bullying, intimidation, or targeted abuse.</li>
            <li>Hate speech, discrimination, or content promoting violence against individuals or groups.</li>
            <li>Nudity, sexually explicit content, sexual exploitation, or inappropriate behaviour.</li>
            <li>Threats, violent behaviour, or encouraging illegal activities.</li>
            <li>Spam, mass messaging, advertising, promotional content, or repetitive unwanted behaviour.</li>
            <li>Scams, phishing attempts, fraud, or misleading users for financial or personal gain.</li>
            <li>Impersonating another person, organisation, or public figure.</li>
            <li>Sharing another person's private or confidential information without permission.</li>
            <li>Attempting to disrupt, abuse, or interfere with the normal operation of the platform.</li>
            <li>Any activity that violates applicable laws or our published platform policies.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 35px;">
          Enforcement Actions
        </h3>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 15px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Reports and moderation actions are reviewed based on the nature and severity of the reported behaviour. Depending on the circumstances, enforcement may include content review, user warnings, temporary restrictions, removal from conversations or rooms, moderator actions such as kick or mute within supported features, temporary suspension, or permanent bans for serious or repeated violations.
        </p>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          We continuously improve our moderation processes to help reduce abuse while maintaining a fair experience for legitimate users. If you encounter behaviour that violates our standards, we encourage you to report it promptly so that appropriate action can be taken. Our goal is to create a community where respectful communication is the expectation, not the exception.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          Privacy, Security & User Responsibility
        </h2>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Privacy and user trust are fundamental to how Wakiee is designed. We believe people should be able to communicate comfortably without sharing unnecessary personal information. We continuously improve our platform, security practices, and moderation processes to help provide a reliable environment for conversations while respecting user privacy.
        </p>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Users are encouraged to avoid sharing sensitive personal information such as home addresses, phone numbers, email addresses, passwords, financial information, government identification documents, or any other confidential data during conversations. Protecting your own privacy is an important part of staying safe online.
        </p>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Wakiee also encourages responsible digital citizenship. If a conversation becomes uncomfortable, abusive, or violates our policies, users should end the conversation immediately and submit a report using the available reporting tools. Community participation helps us identify violations more quickly and contributes to maintaining a respectful environment for everyone.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 35px;">
          Protecting Your Privacy
        </h3>

        <div
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto 35px; text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          <ul style="padding-left: 22px;">
            <li>Think carefully before sharing personal information with people you meet online.</li>
            <li>Never share passwords, banking information, verification codes, or other confidential credentials.</li>
            <li>Report suspicious, abusive, or fraudulent behaviour as soon as possible.</li>
            <li>Leave any conversation that makes you feel uncomfortable or unsafe.</li>
            <li>Respect the privacy and personal boundaries of other users at all times.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          For more information about how information is handled, user responsibilities, and platform policies, please review our <a href="/privacy" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="/terms" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/faq" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Frequently Asked Questions</a>, or <a href="/contact" style="color: #4FA3FF;">Contact Us</a> if you need assistance or wish to report an issue.
        </p>

        <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">
          Our Principles & Ongoing Commitment
        </h2>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Everything we build at Wakiee is guided by a commitment to trust, transparency, privacy, and responsible platform development. We understand that meaningful online communication depends on creating an environment where users feel respected, protected, and confident while interacting with others.
        </p>

        <div
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto 35px; text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          <ul style="padding-left: 22px;">
            <li>
              <strong>User Safety:</strong> Building tools and policies that help create respectful conversations.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Privacy:</strong> Respecting user privacy and encouraging responsible sharing of personal information.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Transparency:</strong> Clearly communicating our policies, moderation approach, and platform expectations.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Continuous Improvement:</strong> Regularly improving platform performance, reliability, moderation systems, and user experience.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Community Respect:</strong> Promoting kindness, inclusion, and constructive communication between people from different backgrounds.
            </li>

            <li>
              <strong>Responsible Innovation:</strong> Developing new features with user safety, accessibility, and long-term platform quality in mind.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p
          style="max-width: 720px; margin: 20px auto; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px;"
        >
          Wakiee continues to evolve through technical improvements, community feedback, and ongoing evaluation of our safety practices. As online communication changes, we remain committed to maintaining a platform that balances accessibility, privacy, responsible moderation, and meaningful conversations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>


